      "prompt": "Enri solved $2 = \\dfrac{22}{x + 4}$ by writing $2 \\times x + 4 = 22$ and got $x = 9$. What is the correct answer?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "$x = 7$" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "$x = 9$ — Enri is right" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "$x = 11$" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "$x = 15$" }
      ],
      "answer": "a",
      "hints": ["It should be $2(x + 4) = 22$."],
      "explanation": "$2(x + 4) = 22 \\Rightarrow x + 4 = 11 \\Rightarrow x = 7$. Check: $\\frac{22}{11} = 2$ ✓"
